  "theorem_statement": "The Seeley-DeWitt spectral action is normalized by the global E6/Weyl root-stabilizer closure. Dividing by |W(E6)|=51840 gives a0/|W|=1/108, a2/|W|=Phi6/(2q^4)=7/162, and a4/|W|=C(k-1,2)/(2q^4)=55/162. Thus a0 is the directed-edge carrier, a2 is the threshold field, and a4 is the radial wedge, all expressed in the same global root-stabilizer units.",
